    "body": "## Motivation\nIn `UnifiedCacheLinkerWrapper.commit_completed_offloads()` (`python/sglang/srt/mem_cache/unified_cache/unified_cache_linker.py`), completed pending offload records are drained FIFO from the head of `self.pending_offloads: list[_PendingOffload]`. Previously, this used `self.pending_offloads.pop(0)` inside a `for _ in range(n):` loop, shifting the remaining list elements left $n$ separate times ($O(n \\cdot L)$ list shifts per batch commit). Additionally, `replace_pending_offload_node()` reassigned `pending.publish_node_ids = [...]` instead of mutating the list in place.\n\n## Modifications\n1. Slice the completed prefix once (`completed = self.pending_offloads[:n]`) and delete it in a single bulk operation (`del self.pending_offloads[:n]`) before iterating over `completed` to mark `external_cache_stored = True` and decrement lock refs.\n2. Update `pending.publish_node_ids[:] = [...]` in place in `replace_pending_offload_node()`.\n\n## Accuracy & Unit Tests\n- Added `test_commit_completed_offloads_batch_fifo_slice` in `test/registered/unit/mem_cache/test_unified_cache_linker.py` verifying partial FIFO prefix draining, lock reference release, and in-place node replacement.\n- `pytest test/registered/unit/mem_cache/test_unified_cache_linker.py`: passed.\n\n## Acknowledgments\nCredit to the SGLang HiCache / UnifiedCache maintainers and contributors for the design and implementation of `UnifiedCacheLinkerWrapper`.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [x] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:warning: [Run #40212892355](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40212892355)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:warning: [Run #40212892198](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40212892198)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:warning: [Run #40212892147](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40212892147)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
